---
layout: base.njk
title: "Nirmaan Outreach: B2B Lead Generation in India"
description: "Find B2B customers in India with researched, personal email and WhatsApp outreach that you approve before anything is sent. Early access."
ogDescription: "B2B lead generation without blasts or bought lists. Nothing is sent until you approve it. Early access."
permalink: "/products/outreach.html"
nav: "products"
scripts: ["tour.js"]
head:
  crumbs: [{ label: "Products", href: "/products.html" }]
  current: "Nirmaan Outreach"
  morph: "product-outreach"
  eyebrow: "Nirmaan Outreach · Early access"
  lines: ["Find the customers", "who need you."]
  accent: 1
  lede: "B2B lead generation without blasts or bought lists. Nirmaan Outreach finds businesses that match the customer you want, looks for a reason to write to each one, and drafts a short message in your voice. <strong>Nothing is sent until you approve it.</strong>"
  glyph: "11111/10001/10101/10001/11111"
  actions:
    - { label: "Ask for early access", href: "/contact.html?product=outreach", style: "primary" }
    - { label: "See it work", href: "#demo" }
cta:
  eyebrow: "Early access"
  lines: ["Tell us who you", "want to reach."]
  text: "We'll tell you honestly whether it fits, how it would find them, and what it would say. We're taking up to three businesses in early access."
  primary: { label: "Ask for early access", href: "/contact.html?product=outreach" }
  secondary: { label: "See it work", href: "#demo" }
problems:
  - title: "Ads"
    text: "You pay for every click. The day you stop paying, the enquiries stop too."
  - title: "Bulk messages"
    text: "Lists and blasts get ignored, reported and blocked, and they take your name down with them."
  - title: "Doing it yourself"
    text: "Personal outreach works. Researching each business and writing to it takes hours you don't have."
features:
  - title: "Finds your customers"
    text: "Searches Google Maps for businesses that match the customer you describe, in the cities you choose."
    glyph: "01110/10001/10001/01110/00011"
  - title: "Looks for a reason to write"
    text: "Reads each business's own website for signs of a problem you solve, like bookings only by phone or a site that isn't set up for phones."
    glyph: "00000/00001/00010/10100/01000"
  - title: "Drafts for you to approve"
    text: "A short first message for each business, in your voice: one specific observation and one small next step. A person approves every message before it's sent. Edit it, approve it, or skip it."
    glyph: "11111/00000/11110/00000/11100"
  - title: "Sends like a person"
    text: "Email goes from your own mailbox, in working hours, one at a time with natural gaps, under your mailbox's daily limit."
    glyph: "00100/00110/11111/00110/00100"
  - title: "WhatsApp, sent by you"
    text: "WhatsApp messages are prepared for you, and you send each one from your own phone. It never sends WhatsApp messages by itself."
    glyph: "11111/10001/10001/11111/01000"
  - title: "Follows up, then listens"
    text: "A short follow-up in the same email thread a few days later. An email reply stops the follow-ups. A “stop” goes on the do-not-contact list, and bounced addresses are retired."
    glyph: "10001/10001/11111/10001/11111"
guards:
  - "Every email ends with a one-line way to opt out, and it can't be edited away."
  - "A “stop” by email puts that business on the do-not-contact list automatically. A “stop” on WhatsApp is added when you mark it. Nobody on the list is contacted again."
  - "Only contact details a business has published itself. No bought lists."
  - "Plain text with your real signature. No tracking pixels."
  - "A few messages per business at most, days apart. An email reply stops the follow-ups as soon as it reaches your inbox."
  - "Every search, draft, approval and send is on record, with who approved it."
audience:
  - "Web and design studios"
  - "Agencies that build for small businesses"
  - "Software teams selling to small businesses"
  - "IT and tech service firms"
setup:
  - title: "Your customer"
    text: "Together we describe who you want to reach, and the problem you solve for them."
  - title: "Your voice"
    text: "We connect a mailbox to send from (ideally one just for outreach), set up your sending domain and signature, and agree how your messages should sound."
  - title: "First campaign"
    text: "We run the first campaign with you and read the first drafts together."
  - title: "It runs"
    text: "It works every day. You approve messages in batches, and we look after it."
faq:
  - q: "Is it ready?"
    a: "It's in early access. We use it for our own outreach, and we're taking up to three businesses now. We set it up and run it with you, and we read the first drafts together. We can't tell you yet what reply rate to expect in your market."
  - q: "Is this spam?"
    a: "It's built to be the opposite. Spam is the same message sent to everyone. Here each message is written for one business, about something on its own website, approved by a person, with a way to opt out. What's allowed depends on who you contact and where, so we agree that with you before you start."
  - q: "Will WhatsApp ban my number?"
    a: "We can't promise that, and nobody honestly can. It never sends WhatsApp messages by itself: you send each one from your own phone. Each message is written for one business, and we start slowly. We'll talk through the risk with you before you use WhatsApp."
  - q: "Do I have to write the messages?"
    a: "No. The research and the first draft are done for you. You read, edit if you like, and approve. Set aside a little time each working day: nothing goes out until you approve it."
  - q: "Does it use AI?"
    a: "Yes, to research businesses and draft messages. A person approves every message, and nothing it reads on the web can send or approve anything."
  - q: "What do you need from me?"
    a: "A mailbox to send from (ideally one just for outreach), a Google account for maps search, your WhatsApp Business number if you want WhatsApp, and an idea of who you want to reach. We'll help you sharpen the last one."
  - q: "What access do you need to my mailbox?"
    a: "An app password for the mailbox you send from. It lets the system send the emails you approve and read the replies. It opens the whole mailbox, so we suggest a separate mailbox just for outreach. You create the password, and you can revoke it at any time."
  - q: "Who owns the leads and messages?"
    a: "You do. You can export your message log as CSV at any time, and when you leave we give you a full export of your prospects, messages and do-not-contact list."
  - q: "Can I use Gmail?"
    a: "Yes, Gmail or Google Workspace. Free Gmail has a lower daily sending limit, so for steady outreach we suggest Workspace."
  - q: "What does it cost?"
    cost: true
  - q: "Do you use it yourselves?"
    a: "Yes. Nirmaan has used it for its own outreach since September 2026. That's why it exists."
---
{%- set m = pricing.products.outreach -%}
{%- set costAnswer -%}
{{ m.setup | inr }} to set up, then {{ m.monthly | inr }} a month, before GST. Early-access clients pay {{ m.earlySetup | inr }} to set up. The monthly fee covers up to {{ m.allowance }} businesses researched a month, hosting and care. Google Maps search is billed to your own Google account, and we show you the expected cost first. The minimum term is {{ m.termMonths }} months.
{%- endset -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "{{ site.url }}/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Products", "item": "{{ site.url }}/products.html" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Nirmaan Outreach", "item": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Service",
      "name": "Nirmaan Outreach",
      "serviceType": "B2B lead generation and outreach",
      "description": {{ description | dump | safe }},
      "url": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}",
      "areaServed": "IN",
      "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization", "name": {{ site.name | dump | safe }}, "url": "{{ site.url }}/" },
      "offers": [
        { "@type": "Offer", "name": "Setup", "price": "{{ m.setup }}", "priceCurrency": "INR" },
        { "@type": "Offer", "name": "Monthly", "priceCurrency": "INR", "priceSpecification": { "@type": "UnitPriceSpecification", "price": "{{ m.monthly }}", "priceCurrency": "INR", "unitText": "MONTH" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</script>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="problem-title">Finding customers is the&nbsp;hard part.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Most small businesses look for new customers in one of three ways. Each works, up to a point.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-problems" role="list">
      {%- for p in problems %}
      <li class="mk-problem" data-reveal style="--d: {{ loop.index0 }}">
        <h3 class="mk-problem__title">{{ p.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ p.text }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="mk-answer display" data-reveal>Nirmaan Outreach does the research and the first draft. <span class="accent">You keep the&nbsp;judgement.</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">See it work</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="demo-title">One campaign, start to&nbsp;finish.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section__text">Seven steps, from a goal in plain words to a reply in your inbox. Press any step, or let it play.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="tour__note mono">Illustration with sample businesses. Not real data.</p>

    <div class="tour" data-tour>
      <div class="tour__bar">
        <div class="tour__steps" aria-label="Campaign steps">
          {%- set steps = ["Goal", "Find", "Check", "Draft", "Approve", "Listen", "Learn"] %}
          {%- for s in steps %}
          <button class="tour__step" type="button" id="tour-tab-{{ loop.index }}" aria-controls="tour-beat-{{ loop.index }}"><span class="mono">0{{ loop.index }}</span> {{ s }}</button>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="tour__controls">
          <button class="tour__ctrl mono" type="button" data-tour-toggle aria-pressed="false">Pause</button>
          <button class="tour__ctrl mono" type="button" data-tour-replay>Replay</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tour__progress" aria-hidden="true"><span data-tour-progress></span></div>

      <div class="tour__stage">
        {#- 1. Goal -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-1" aria-labelledby="tour-title-1">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-1"><span class="mono">01</span> Write the goal in plain words.</h3>
            <p>Say you run a web studio and want clinics as clients. It turns your goal into a plan you can check and edit: what to search for, where, and what the first messages lead with.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">New campaign</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 0">Goal</p>
              <p class="console__input" data-i style="--i: 1">Dental and skin clinics in Ahmedabad and Surat that still book appointments by phone.</p>
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 2">Plan</p>
              <ul class="console__rows" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 3"><span>dental clinic</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 4"><span>dental clinic</span><span class="mono">Surat</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 5"><span>skin clinic</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 6"><span>skin clinic</span><span class="mono">Surat</span></li>
              </ul>
              <p class="console__note" data-i style="--i: 7">First messages lead with: <b>booking online, day and night</b></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 2. Find -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-2" aria-labelledby="tour-title-2">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-2"><span class="mono">02</span> It finds businesses that fit.</h3>
            <p>It searches maps for businesses in your cities, a little every day. Each business appears once, with where it was found.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">Found today</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <ul class="console__rows" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 0"><span>Riverside Dental Studio</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 1"><span>Lotus Skin Clinic</span><span class="mono">Surat · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 2"><span>Northgate Dental Care</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 3"><span>Banyan Skin &amp; Hair</span><span class="mono">Surat · maps</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 4"><span>Meridian Smiles</span><span class="mono">Ahmedabad · maps</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 3. Check -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-3" aria-labelledby="tour-title-3">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-3"><span class="mono">03</span> It looks for a reason to write.</h3>
            <p>It reads the business's own website and checks the fit. Businesses that don't fit are left out.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">riverside-dental.example</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 0">What the site shows</p>
              <ul class="console__signals" role="list">
                <li class="is-yes" data-i style="--i: 1">Appointments by phone call only</li>
                <li class="is-yes" data-i style="--i: 2">No way to book after hours</li>
                <li class="is-yes" data-i style="--i: 3">Not set up for phones</li>
                <li class="is-no" data-i style="--i: 4">Online payments: not needed</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="console__verdict" data-i style="--i: 5"><b>Good fit.</b> Worth a message about booking online.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 4. Draft -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-4" aria-labelledby="tour-title-4">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-4"><span class="mono">04</span> It drafts a message in your voice.</h3>
            <p>Short, first person, one specific observation and one small next step. Every email ends with a way to opt out.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">Draft · email</b></div>
            <div class="console__body console__mail">
              <p class="mono console__meta" data-i style="--i: 0">To: hello@riverside-dental.example</p>
              <p class="console__subject" data-i style="--i: 1">Evening appointments at Riverside</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 2">Hello Dr. Mehta,</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 3"><mark>I noticed appointments at Riverside can only be booked by phone, so patients who call after hours can't get through.</mark> A simple booking page could take those bookings while you're closed.</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 4">Would a 15-minute call this week be useful?</p>
              <p data-i style="--i: 5">Asha, Studio Sample</p>
              <p class="console__optout" data-i style="--i: 6">Not relevant? Reply “stop” and we won’t contact you again.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 5. Approve -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-5" aria-labelledby="tour-title-5">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-5"><span class="mono">05</span> You approve. Then it sends like a person.</h3>
            <p>Email goes from your mailbox in working hours, one at a time. WhatsApp is ready for you to send from your phone in one tap.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">Waiting for you</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <ul class="console__rows console__rows--queue" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 0"><span>Riverside Dental Studio</span><span class="console__chip is-done mono">Approved</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 1"><span class="console__sub">Email · sends at 11:42, working hours</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 2"><span>Lotus Skin Clinic</span><span class="console__chip mono">Send on WhatsApp</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 3"><span class="console__sub">One tap from your phone</span></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 4"><span>Meridian Smiles</span><span class="console__chip mono">Read, edit, approve</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 6. Listen -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-6" aria-labelledby="tour-title-6">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-6"><span class="mono">06</span> It listens to replies.</h3>
            <p>A reply stops the follow-ups, and you can turn it into a lead in one click. Anyone who replies “stop” goes on the do-not-contact list.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">Inbox</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <div class="console__reply" data-i style="--i: 0">
                <p class="mono console__meta">Riverside Dental Studio · Re: Evening appointments</p>
                <p>“Yes, call me on Thursday after 6.”</p>
              </div>
              <ul class="console__events" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 1">Follow-up cancelled</li>
                <li class="is-blue" data-i style="--i: 2">Ready to add as a lead</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="console__reply" data-i style="--i: 3">
                <p class="mono console__meta">Northgate Dental Care · Re: Online bookings</p>
                <p>“stop”</p>
              </div>
              <ul class="console__events" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 4">Added to do-not-contact</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        {#- 7. Learn -#}
        <section class="tour__beat" id="tour-beat-7" aria-labelledby="tour-title-7">
          <div class="tour__caption">
            <h3 class="tour__title" id="tour-title-7"><span class="mono">07</span> Every week, it shows what's working.</h3>
            <p>Replies by segment, city and channel. Once there's enough to go on, it moves effort toward what gets replies and tells you what it changed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="console" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="console__bar"><b class="mono">Weekly review</b></div>
            <div class="console__body">
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 0">Replies by segment</p>
              <ul class="console__bars" role="list">
                <li data-i style="--i: 1"><span>Dental clinics</span><i style="--w: 0.9"></i></li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 2"><span>Skin clinics</span><i style="--w: 0.5"></i></li>
              </ul>
              <p class="console__label mono" data-i style="--i: 3">Next week</p>
              <ul class="console__events" role="list">
                <li class="is-blue" data-i style="--i: 4">More dental clinics</li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 5">Surat searched first</li>
                <li data-i style="--i: 6">A little more email, a little less WhatsApp</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="who-title">
  <div class="wrap mk-split">
    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Who it's for</p>
      <h2 class="section__title display" id="who-title">Businesses that win work by&nbsp;talking.</h2>
      <p class="section__text">For businesses whose offer fixes something you can see on a customer's website. It isn't for promotional blasts to the public.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mk-audience" role="list" data-reveal>
      {%- for a in audience %}
      <li>{{ a }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head section__head--split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
        <h2 class="section__title display" id="features-title">The research and the writing, done for&nbsp;you.</h2>
